# Citation metadata: GitHub shows a "Cite this repository" box from this file, and
# Zenodo reads it when it archives a release. Update `version` and `date-released`
# at every release (and add the Zenodo `doi:` once the first archive exists).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PhysicsLibrary in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PhysicsLibrary (ZaksPhysicsLibrary): data processing and analysis library for PyAT"
type: software
version: "2026.9.24"
date-released: "2026-09-24"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zakgm2/PhysicsLibrary"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/ZaksPhysicsLibrary/"
url: "https://github.com/zakgm2/PhysicsLibrary"
abstract: >-
  Data processing and analysis library behind PyAT (Python Analysis Tool): fibre-photometry
  (TDT) motion and photobleaching correction, dF/F, event-locked z-score PETH, peak finding,
  AUC, FFT and curve fitting, plus loaders for Oxysoft NIRS, generic tabular data and Terranova
  EFNMR files. It contains no GUI code of its own.
keywords:
  - fibre photometry
  - neuroscience
  - signal processing
  - dF/F
  - PETH
authors:
  - family-names: "Grand Maison"
    given-names: "Z."   # as in the app's APA citation; spell out if you prefer
    # affiliation: "Your university / lab"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
